      r"""From the official solution: the 5.00 nC charge is 3.0 cm away and gives $E_+ = k\frac{5.00\times10^{-9}}{(0.030)^2} = 5.0\times10^4$ N/C along $+\hat\imath$. The −20.00 nC charge sits at $(0.040, 0.020)$ m and gives a field pointing TOWARD it: $$E_- = k\frac{20.00\times10^{-9}}{0.040^2 + 0.020^2} = 9.0\times10^4\ \text{N/C} \;\Rightarrow\; (8.0\times10^4\,\hat\imath + 4.0\times10^4\,\hat\jmath)\ \text{N/C}.$$ Sum: $\vec E = (1.3\times10^5\,\hat\imath + 4.0\times10^4\,\hat\jmath)$ N/C.""",
